{"kind":"request","text":"Stop the stale short-circuit from hiding kept promises. In projectCommitments (spike/internal/workroom/fold.go), the case stale[request] || stale[promise] returns status stale before reports are consulted, leaving the commitment's report empty and waiting_on set to the performer. A promise that was reported and requester-ratified is then indistinguishable on the board from one never started, and names the performer as the party being waited on. Todays closure sweep found six such phantoms; every one had a filed verdict, and no act by the named actor can clear the false obligation. Child of the commitment-projection request this rests on: compute the report and terminal state first, and render staleness as a qualifier on the row rather than a status that suppresses it.","body":{"conditions":"A commitment whose promise has a non-retired report projects that report and its terminal state even when the request or promise is stale; staleness appears as a distinct qualifier; a regression test pins a reported-and-ratified commitment under a stale request; existing stale semantics for genuinely unreported commitments unchanged.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}